              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Catjaq"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The first time I made this according to recipe and my family of picky eaters loved it. But then I sprinkled southwest seasoning on chicken breast and cooked and cut into bite-sized pieces, added it to the mix and added extra cheese on top, and they devoured it."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "AEMAZA"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent, fast and easy. I added some salsa to make it a bit more saucy, chunked the cheese and used a bit of Pepper Jack too, since we like more cheese and spicy foods...awesome. I'll be sending this recipe to my son in college who needs some easy recipes...this is a DEFINITE keeper.",
            "datePublished": "2012-10-12T17:45:32.730Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Bill Howard"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made some tweaks including use of butter instead of margerine, draining some juice from the tomatoes, use of Goya Adobo instead of salt and increasing the amount to 1 tsp, upped the cheese to about 3 cups (no one sells 2 1/2 C packages), and greasing the pan. I assembled the dish by tossing the penne with the butter to coat, then added the tomatoes, then the sugar and adobo seasoning and finally the cheese. I'm with the others to cook this for 30 minutes. I sprinkled some additional cheese on the finished dish. I had 4C on hand. Next time, I'll rethink the seasoning as adding sugar made no sense to me. Also go with more cheese (4 cups).",
            "datePublished": "2025-10-09T19:45:04.923Z"
          },
